{
  "example": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.agent_config`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`\n\nThis Bedrock configuration selects a model, AWS profile, and region for the\ndomain's cache:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse trust_but_verify::agent::AgentConfig;\nuse trust_but_verify::agent::BedrockConfig;\nuse trust_but_verify::domain::ValidationCache;\n\nlet config = AgentConfig::Bedrock(\n    BedrockConfig::new(\"us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5\".into())\n        .aws_profile(\"development\".into())\n        .region(\"us-east-1\".into()),\n);\nlet cache = ValidationCache::with_agent(config);\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.setup` describes a concrete case. A Bedrock `AgentConfig` has a model, an AWS profile and a region, and `ValidationCache::with_agent(config)` attaches it to the domain's cache. The expected behavior is that the cache selects that agent. The cited requirements add that backend setup is deferred, that criteria obtain the agent through the cache, and that the SDK does not persist the configuration.\n\nThe one `{test}` reference to the example is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted]`. It checks each outcome:\n- **Same configuration as the example:** It builds an `AgentConfig::Bedrock` with `BedrockConfig::new(\"us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5\")`, `.aws_profile(\"development\")` and `.region(\"us-east-1\")`. These are the example's values.\n- **Cache selects the agent:** It sets the `TestDomain` cache with `ValidationCache::with_agent(config.clone())`. It then asserts that `peer.cache().agent.as_ref().unwrap().config == config`, so the cache holds the supplied configuration.\n- **Shared by domain clones:** `Arc::ptr_eq` on the agents of `domain` and its clone `peer` shows one agent is shared.\n- **Deferred backend setup:** `validation::refresh_evidence` runs a deterministic `Question(false)` criterion against this Bedrock-configured cache. It succeeds with output false, even though a real Bedrock backend with profile \"development\" would need credentials. The test therefore shows that no backend is set up until an agent request is awaited. The sibling test `configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors` asserts `provider.get().is_none()` directly for OpenAI.\n- **Not persisted:** It serializes the stored evidence record. It asserts there is no `backend` field and that the JSON contains neither \"development\" nor \"claude-sonnet\".\n\nI found no unresolved gap. The `assert_eq!` compares the stored config with a clone of the input, so it checks that the cache keeps the configuration, not that the builders set the fields. The builder behavior belongs to the `BedrockConfig` requirements, not this example. The test checks every behavior the example and its cited requirements state.",
  "references": "7c7524ee8e51af918c33943dcb55e9936d8e326b278323071bdbeabdfe57c6a0",
